mimid-seed: give local users of a mimid provider a client and KeyPackages,
so that a peer's protocol-07 §5.2 keyMaterial request for them succeeds
(bead mimid-1wgh.46.10). mimid's JMAP surface cannot upload KeyPackages
yet, so until it can, no local user exists without this (decision
mimid-1wgh.7.9). Not run in CI.

Layout
  Cargo.toml    standalone crate (own [workspace]): mimid crates by relative
                path, plus a copy of the root Cargo.toml [patch] section
                (keep the two in step)
  src/main.rs   mimid-seed, the seeder
  src/bin/mimid-seed-probe.rs
                sends one keyMaterial request per user, as a peer would, and
                checks the KeyPackages that come back. Each successful probe
                consumes a one-time KeyPackage.

What it stores, per user mimi://<domain>/u/<name>
  - one client Identity (BasicCredential = the user URI, Ed25519 key),
    minted once and reloaded on later runs; its client URI is
    mimi://<domain>/d/<base32 SHA-256 of the key> (decision mimid-1wgh.7.8)
  - the user's JMAP account, if missing (no bearer token is issued)
  - N one-time KeyPackages (default 20) and one last-resort KeyPackage,
    each through KeyPackages::upload_key_package, the validated upload path
  - in --state-dir (default <database>.seed-state), mode 0700/0600:
      <name>/identity.json  user URI, client URI, signature public key
      <name>/mls.sqlite     mimi-mls Store: the signature private key and
                            every KeyPackage's private keys, in the clear
    A later tool reloads the client with mimi_mls::Identity::load(user URI,
    public key, Store::open(mls.sqlite)) and can join from a Welcome.
    Keep this directory: without it the seeded users cannot join groups.

Rerunning tops each client up to N unexpired one-time KeyPackages, and
replaces the last-resort one if it ends before --valid-through. A user with
clients in the database but no state in --state-dir is refused, rather than
given a second identity.

KeyPackages have OpenMLS's default lifetime: one hour in the past to 84
days ahead. The tool stops if one would end before the end of
--valid-through (default 2026-11-17, UTC).

Running next to mimid
  Safe with mimid stopped or running: the database is WAL with a 5 s busy
  timeout, uploads take the write lock with BEGIN IMMEDIATE, and keyMaterial
  reads the KeyPackage tables on every request. The tool refuses to run
  unless the database exists, is owned by the user running it (so no -wal
  or -shm file ends up unreadable to mimid), and has exactly the migrations
  of the mimid revision the tool was built from, so it never migrates a
  database under another mimid. Build it from the deployed revision.

Variables
  MIMID   this repository's root
  CACHE   ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}; use a private CARGO_TARGET_DIR
          under it, not a shared target directory

Build
  export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CACHE/mimid-seed-target
  (cd $MIMID/tools/interop/seed && cargo build --release)

Seed (as the user that runs mimid)
  $CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/mimid-seed --config /etc/mimid/config.toml \
     --users alice,carol,dave [--count 20] [--state-dir DIR] \
     [--valid-through 2026-11-17]

Probe (consumes one KeyPackage per user)
  $CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/mimid-seed-probe --target-domain <domain> \
     --target-url <mimid base URL> --from <any other domain> --users alice
  The requester is mimi://<from>/u/seed-probe and the room
  mimi://<from>/r/seed-probe, so the From domain is the room's authority.

Local test
  A mimid with domain mimid.test, base_url http://127.0.0.1:<port>, a temp
  database and [peers] "peer.test" = "http://127.0.0.1:9": start it once,
  seed, then probe with --target-domain mimid.test --from peer.test.
